### Kevalon ERP Module 6: Supplier API requests
@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000/api/supplier
@accessToken = YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN
@companyId = YOUR_COMPANY_ID
@supplierId = YOUR_SUPPLIER_ID
@payableAccountId = OPTIONAL_COA_ACCOUNT_ID

### Create supplier (payableAccountId is optional; no COA is created automatically)
POST {{baseUrl}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "companyId": "{{companyId}}",
  "name": "ABC Traders",
  "code": "SUP-001",
  "gstin": "22AAAAA0000A1Z5",
  "pan": "AAAAA0000A",
  "email": "supplier@example.com",
  "phone": "9876543210",
  "billingAddress": {
    "line1": "21 Market Road",
    "city": "Ahmedabad",
    "state": "Gujarat",
    "pincode": "380001",
    "country": "India"
  },
  "contactPerson": "Mr. Supplier"
}

### List suppliers. Optional filters: search, isActive, page and limit.
GET {{baseUrl}}?companyId={{companyId}}&search=ABC&isActive=true&page=1&limit=20
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Get one supplier
GET {{baseUrl}}/{{supplierId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Update supplier / optionally link a payable COA belonging to this company
PUT {{baseUrl}}/{{supplierId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "ABC Traders Pvt. Ltd.",
  "payableAccountId": "{{payableAccountId}}",
  "isActive": true
}

### Supplier payable ledger (currently a zeroed, read-only placeholder)
GET {{baseUrl}}/{{supplierId}}/ledger?companyId={{companyId}}&from=2026-04-01&to=2027-03-31
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
